---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import RelatedLinks from '../components/RelatedLinks.astro';
import MedicalDisclaimer from '../components/MedicalDisclaimer.astro';

const title = 'Normal GFR by Age Chart: eGFR Normal Range for Adults';
const description =
	'A normal eGFR is usually above 90. Average eGFR falls from 116 at ages 20-29 to 75 at age 70+. See the full chart by age and what a lower number can mean.';
---

<Layout
	title={title}
	description={description}
	modified="2026-11-03"
	breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Normal GFR by Age', href: '/normal-gfr-by-age' }]}
	schema={[
		{
			'@type': 'Article',
			headline: title,
			description,
			mainEntityOfPage: { '@id': 'https://gfrcalc.com/normal-gfr-by-age#webpage' },
			dateModified: '2026-11-03',
			datePublished: '2026-10-23',
			author: { '@id': 'https://gfrcalc.com/#organization' },
			publisher: { '@id': 'https://gfrcalc.com/#organization' },
			image: 'https://gfrcalc.com/og-image.png',
		},
	]}
>
	<article class="container-page py-14 sm:py-20">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
			<Breadcrumbs trail={[{ name: 'Normal GFR by Age' }]} />
			<h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
				Normal GFR by age: eGFR normal range chart
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				A normal eGFR for adults is usually above 90 mL/min/1.73m&sup2;, and it falls gradually with
				age. On average it is about 116 in your 20s, 99 in your 40s, 85 in your 60s, and 75 from age 70.
				An eGFR below 60 for more than three months meets the definition of CKD at any age. Use it
				for context alongside your own result from the
				<a href="/" class="text-link hover:text-link-deep">GFR calculator</a>.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-faint">Last updated November 3, 2026</p>

			<h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Average GFR by age</h2>
			<div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md border border-hairline">
				<table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
					<caption class="sr-only">Average GFR by age group, in mL/min/1.73m&sup2;</caption>
					<thead>
						<tr class="border-b border-hairline bg-hairline-soft">
							<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">Age (years)</th>
							<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">Average GFR (mL/min/1.73m&sup2;)</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline">
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">20&ndash;29</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">116</td></tr>
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">30&ndash;39</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">107</td></tr>
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">40&ndash;49</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">99</td></tr>
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">50&ndash;59</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">93</td></tr>
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">60&ndash;69</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">85</td></tr>
						<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-ink">70+</th><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-body">75</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-faint">
				Values are population averages as published by the National Kidney Foundation, not
				pass/fail cut-offs. Individual healthy values vary widely around these averages.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Why GFR declines with age</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				After about age 30 to 40, GFR falls on average by roughly 1 mL/min/1.73m&sup2; per year.
				The kidneys lose some functioning nephrons over time, and blood vessels stiffen. The
				rate of decline differs greatly between people. Diabetes, high blood pressure, obesity,
				smoking, and some medicines speed it up.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Is a lower GFR at an older age still a problem?</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				An eGFR in the 60s is common in people over 65 and is not always accompanied by kidney
				damage. Guidelines still classify an eGFR below 60 for more than three months as
				<a href="/ckd-stages" class="text-link hover:text-link-deep">CKD stage G3 or worse</a>
				regardless of age, because the risk of complications rises with lower GFR. How much that
				matters for an individual depends on albuminuria, the trend over time, and other health
				conditions, which is a conversation for a clinician.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Other things that affect your result</h2>
			<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				<li><strong>Muscle mass.</strong> Creatinine comes from muscle, so very muscular people can look worse than they are and people with low muscle mass can look better.</li>
				<li><strong>Diet and hydration.</strong> A large cooked-meat meal or dehydration can raise creatinine temporarily.</li>
				<li><strong>Sex.</strong> Equations use different constants for male and female creatinine levels.</li>
				<li><strong>Equation choice.</strong> CKD-EPI 2021, CKD-EPI 2009, and MDRD can give different numbers for the same person. See our <a href="/methodology" class="text-link hover:text-link-deep">methodology</a>.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Sources</h2>
			<ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
				<li><a href="https://www.kidney.org/kidney-topics/estimated-glomerular-filtration-rate-egfr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:text-link-deep">National Kidney Foundation: Estimated Glomerular Filtration Rate (eGFR)</a>.</li>
				<li>KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Evaluation and Management of CKD. <em>Kidney International</em>. 2024;105(4S):S117&ndash;S314.</li>
			</ul>

			<div class="mt-12"><MedicalDisclaimer /></div>
			<RelatedLinks only={['/egfr-results', '/', '/ckd-stages', '/egfr-blood-test']} />
		</div>
	</article>
</Layout>
